fix: resolve AppHost project paths using AppContext.BaseDirectory

CATEGORY: Bug Fix / Infrastructure

DESCRIPTION:
- Fixed Aspire AppHost failing to find project files by using AppContext.BaseDirectory
- Previously used Directory.GetCurrentDirectory() which caused lookups in bin/Debug folder
- Now dynamically resolves server directory from binary location
- Upgraded from .NET 10.0 preview to stable .NET 9.0

CHANGES:
- Modified AppHost/Program.cs to use AppContext.BaseDirectory for path resolution
- Path calculation: AppContext.BaseDirectory -> navigate up from bin/Debug/net9.0/
- Updated global.json to use .NET 9.0 (stable release) with rollForward: latestFeature

FIXES:
- "Project file 'bin/Debug/net9.0/gateway/ApiGateway/ApiGateway.csproj' was not found" error
- Aspire now correctly finds all microservice projects at runtime
- Removed dependency on .NET 10 preview

TESTING:
- AppHost builds successfully with .NET 9 SDK
- Path resolution verified for all services and gateway
